Thanks @hkdobrev for the feedback. Right now, this is not possible as part of instantsearch.js but we can definitely work something out to have an option. In the meantime, you could monkeypatch the widget and check the number of pages, like so:

``` js
var container = document.querySelector('#pagination');
var paginationWidget = instantsearch.widgets.pagination({container: container});
var oldRender = paginationWidget.render;
paginationWidget.render = function(params) {
  var currentState = params.results;
  if(currentState.nbPages===0) container.style.display='none';
  else container.style.display = 'block';
  oldRender.call(this, arguments);
}
search.addWidget(paginationWidget);
```

@pixelastic Thanks for spending the time on this.

I think the option name `minPages` would not represent the behaviour correctly and it would bring confusion when it's being compared with the semantics behind `maxPages`.

Having a function for `autoHideContainer` - basically a hook, is always useful. This is something very similar to what is considered for the search box widget with https://github.com/algolia/instantsearch.js/issues/776#issuecomment-172900988.

@hkdobrev Using the `render` event you should be able to hide/show the pagination: https://community.algolia.com/instantsearch.js/documentation/#events

I do not think we need any new API entry to deal with this case. Given your preference you might or might not want to hide the pagination.

Still, being able to use a function as for the autoHideContainer seems like a nice idea, can you draft a new issue about it? Much like the #817
